# Lecturia Project Rules

## About This Project
Lecturia is an educational platform where lecturers upload course materials and students can chat with an AI assistant that answers questions based on those materials (using RAG - Retrieval Augmented Generation).

## User Roles
- **Lecturer**: Creates courses, uploads documents (PDF, Word, text), manages students
- **Student**: Joins courses via invite code, chats with AI about course content

## Tech Stack
- **Framework**: Next.js 16 with App Router (React 19)
- **Language**: TypeScript (strict mode)
- **Database & Auth**: Supabase (PostgreSQL + Auth + Storage)
- **Styling**: Tailwind CSS v4
- **UI Components**: shadcn/ui (Radix primitives)
- **AI/LLM**: OpenAI for embeddings and chat
- **Forms**: React Hook Form + Zod validation

## Project Structure
```
src/
├── app/              # Next.js App Router pages and API routes
│   ├── api/          # Backend API endpoints
│   ├── lecturer/     # Lecturer dashboard pages
│   └── student/      # Student dashboard pages
├── components/       # React components
│   ├── ui/           # shadcn/ui base components
│   ├── lecturer/     # Lecturer-specific components
│   └── student/      # Student-specific components
├── lib/              # Utility functions and configurations
│   ├── supabase/     # Supabase client setup (client.ts, server.ts, admin.ts)
│   ├── llm/          # LLM integrations (OpenAI, Anthropic)
│   ├── embeddings/   # Text embedding generation
│   ├── rag/          # RAG search functionality
│   └── file-processors/  # PDF, Word, text file parsing
└── types/            # TypeScript type definitions
```

## Coding Guidelines

### General
- Always use TypeScript with proper types - avoid `any`
- Use async/await instead of .then() chains
- Handle errors gracefully with try/catch blocks
- Add meaningful comments for complex logic

### React & Next.js
- Use Server Components by default (no 'use client' unless needed)
- Add 'use client' only for: hooks, browser APIs, event handlers, state
- Use the App Router patterns (not Pages Router)
- API routes go in `src/app/api/` using route.ts files

### Supabase
- Client-side: use `createClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/client`
- Server-side: use `createClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/server`
- Admin operations: use `createAdminClient()` from `@/lib/supabase/admin`
- Always check for auth errors and handle them

### Styling
- Use Tailwind CSS utility classes
- Use shadcn/ui components from `@/components/ui/`
- Follow existing component patterns for consistency
- Use the `cn()` utility for conditional classes

## Communication Style
Always explain code changes as if I'm not a developer - I'm learning while building this project. Include:
- What the change does in plain English
- Why it's needed
- Any important concepts I should understand
